    description      = "Detects a confirmation-bypass sentence, a Cyrillic homoglyph of that sentence, a credential path next to curl or wget, ignore-previous-instructions next to a fetch, or a listed API token next to a fetch and a URL whose host is not that token's vendor. A pipe into a shell matches unless the whole command is one listed first-party installer line. The sentence list is generated from larc_seraph.phrases. A Markdown heading, a table row, a backticked status label, a known permission flag, or a prohibition such as never bypass permissions does not match. A read-only action does not match unless a high-risk action is on the same line. A paraphrase that names its own scope (approval is not required for read-only git commands) is judged with its own sentence, and a prohibition worded may not, cannot, is not allowed to, or under no circumstances does not match. Path-scoped variant. It requires the filepath external and is not for YARA-Forge."
